This project implements the ntfy HTTP notification protocol in Rust.
It is an independent implementation, not an official ntfy release.

The web/ directory is the ntfy web application, copied without functional
changes from https://github.com/binwiederhier/ntfy at commit
59f9931f0f365f1e33871ed9d641b33e8039c190 (2026-11-05 retrieval).
Copyright Philipp C. Heckel and ntfy contributors.
Used under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE.

The Rust server uses a dedicated message-cache schema and supports standard
ntfy authentication and Web Push SQLite schemas.
See docs/compatibility.md before replacing an existing ntfy server.

SQLite authentication/Web Push schemas, migrations and message-cache test
fixtures are derived from ntfy v2.37.2
(commit 05109571fd0931affb6f92b17bbfd62c4d2ea68a), licensed under Apache-2.0.
